#: ../../source/reference/vector4.rst:13
msgid ""
"Vectors are one of the main building blocks of 4D representation and "
"drawing. They consist of three coordinates, traditionally called x, y, z "
"and w."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/vector4.rst:15
msgid ""
"The Vector4 class can also be used to represent vertices in 4D space. We "
"therefore do not need to provide a separate vertex class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/vector4.rst:18
msgid ""
"Note: By design values in the Vector4 instance are stored as float. This "
"means that on platforms where the areal arguments to Vector4 functions "
"are represented by double values, it is possible to lose precision."
msgstr ""

